# The beman.specgen revision that generates the committed wording fragments.
#
# `make wording-check` regenerates every fragment and diffs it against what is
# committed, so the answer depends on which specgen ran.  CI checks out exactly
# this ref; a developer regenerating locally should have a specgen built from
# it, or `make wording` will produce a diff that is the tool's and not theirs.
#
# A branch name tracks specgen's head, which is right while the two repositories
# are moving together and wrong the moment a specgen change lands that this
# paper has not adopted.  Pin a commit SHA here instead as soon as the pair
# stops moving together -- the file is read verbatim by `git checkout`, so a SHA
# works with no other change.
main
